Ratchet

A background agent that continuously:

Collects metrics

Detects anomalies

Diagnoses cause

Fixes automatically (if safe)

Sends report

So it behaves like:

“self-healing device supervisor”

Core architecture (simple but powerful)
Components
1. Metrics Tool

Collect:

CPU %

memory %

disk %

temperature

battery/voltage (optional)

logs

Linux commands:

top / psutil
free
df
vcgencmd measure_temp (Raspberry Pi)
journalctl / dmesg

Python tool:

get_system_metrics()

2. Log Tool

Reads:

syslog

app logs

errors

Expose:

read_recent_logs()

3. Action Tool (very important)

Agent can actually act:

restart_service(service)
kill_process(pid)
clear_cache()
reboot_device()


This makes it autonomous → judges love this.

4. Alert Tool
send_telegram()
send_email()
write_report()

5. AI Agent (brain)

Responsibilities:

reason over metrics

explain root cause

decide action

call tools

Workflow logic

Think like this:

Every 60s:
   → get metrics
   → if abnormal:
         read logs
         diagnose
         fix
         notify

Example reasoning:

CPU = 98%
Top process = python app
Memory leak pattern
→ restart service
→ send report


That’s real “agentic behavior”.

